  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Heidenhain Klartext post (`assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps`) writes a section's smoothing ask (`PARAM Smoothing` / `SmoothingMode`, #616) as cycle 32 TOLERANCE. Before this change, the post refused each smoothing ask. This is the next slice of #4095: the Klartext post now reads the resolver flags `g62Mode` and `g62TMaxUm` (#4226). Until now, only the DIN/ISO post read them.\n\n- The blocks come after `M3` and `M8`/`M9`, before the first move of the section:\n  - `CYCL DEF 32.0 TOLERANCE`\n  - `CYCL DEF 32.1 T<mm>` (1 µm grid, the same grid as the DIN/ISO `G62`)\n  - `CYCL DEF 32.2 HSC-MODE:<0|1> TA0`, only where `g62Mode` permits it: `yes`, or `option2` with option 2 in `installed_options`. `0` is finish, `1` is rough. The post moves no rotary axis, so `TA` is 0.\n- The section end resets the cycle with `CYCL DEF 32.0 TOLERANCE` and `CYCL DEF 32.1` (no T), before `M9` and `M5`. Thus no tolerance goes into the next operation.\n- The post refuses by name:\n  - a T above the largest T of the profile (`g62TMaxUm`);\n  - a positive T that rounds to T0 (the control reads T 0 as the machine builder's tolerance);\n  - a profile with no cycle 32;\n  - a rough ask where `32.2 HSC-MODE` cannot be written (the post sets `failOnWarning`, so a warning would also stop it);\n  - a mode with no tolerance, a mode that is not finish or rough, and a tolerance that is not a positive number.\n- Source: iTNC 530 Klartext user manual 533 190-22 (NC 340 49x-03), section 8.10 \"TOLERANCE (Cycle 32)\", pages 509-511. The post header cites this manual already.\n- One form is inferred: the manual prints no reset block. The post writes `CYCL DEF 32.1` with no T, which is what the manual's NO ENT answer leaves. This is the same inference as the bare `G62` reset of the DIN/ISO post. The decision file says this.\n- Decisions and dropped options: `docs/decisions/4095-klartext-cycle-32.md`.\n\n## Fehlmann Picomax 55 (iTNC 530, NC 340490-03, profile itnc-49x)\n\nThe machine file lists no installed options. Thus:\n- a finish ask posts `CYCL DEF 32.0 TOLERANCE` and `CYCL DEF 32.1 T<mm>` only;\n- a rough ask is refused: `smoothing mode rough: controller profile itnc-49x takes CYCL DEF 32.2 HSC-MODE only with software option 2 (HSC machining), which the machine file does not list; ask for finish smoothing, or none - refused, not posted`;\n- the largest T is 10 mm.\n\nA program with no smoothing ask is byte-identical. The `picomax.nc` and `picomax_cycles.nc` goldens and the refusal goldens did not change.\n\nExample (from the new golden `picomax_smoothing.nc`, a finish ask of 0.02 mm, then a section with no ask):\n\n```\n25 M3\n26 M9\n27 CYCL DEF 32.0 TOLERANCE\n28 CYCL DEF 32.1 T0.02\n29 L X+10 Y+0 R0 FMAX\n...\n38 L X+15 Y+0 Z+10 R0 FMAX\n39 CYCL DEF 32.0 TOLERANCE\n40 CYCL DEF 32.1\n41 M9\n42 M5\n```\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nBinary `script_goldens` (crate `camcraft-post`), suite module `script_heidenhain_klartext`, new module `crates/post/tests/klartext/smoothing_tests.rs` (it joins the existing suite; no new test binary):\n- `smoothing_tests::klartext_smoothing_posts_on_the_picomax_golden` (new golden `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/heidenhain-klartext/picomax_smoothing.nc`)\n- `smoothing_tests::a_finish_ask_writes_t_only_and_the_section_end_resets_it`\n- `smoothing_tests::option_2_writes_hsc_mode_for_finish_and_rough`\n- `smoothing_tests::each_klartext_smoothing_refusal_names_its_cause`\n- `smoothing_tests::the_t_range_bounds_post_on_the_picomax`\n- `unsupported_motion_or_missing_setup_data_is_refused`: its smoothing case is now a rough ask (refused on the Picomax), because a finish ask posts now. The case count is the same.\n\n## Gate results\n\nFinal head `bf7c0d068` (it merges `origin/main` `4d891498e`; the merge moved the Klartext suite into `script_goldens`, #3188).\n\n- Mac lane (`--needs app --pool`), log `gate-4095-bf7c0d0-app.log`:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 34 steps, 34 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The plan has `post suites: script_goldens`, the app suites `conformance` and `klartext_builtin`, and `gcode suites: klartext`.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work --test smoothing`: 47 + 1 + 1 + 8 passed, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- winbuild lane (`camcraft-post`, head `bf7c0d068`), log `gate-4095-bf7c0d0-post.log`: `script_goldens` 445 passed (the five `script_heidenhain_klartext::smoothing_tests::*` tests and `unsupported_motion_or_missing_setup_data_is_refused` included); `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib heidenhain` 14 passed; clippy `camcraft-post` clean.\n- Light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`): 6 steps, 6 ok. It ran on head `5f791786e` (before the merge of main; the code under test is the same). Log `gate-4095-5f79178-app.log`. On that head, the quick gate had one red step: `example_catalog` `catalog_3d_rough_finish::rebuilds` and `::regenerates` stopped at their 60 s time budget under load (open issue #3975). On the final head the same tests passed.\n- The new golden `picomax_smoothing.nc` was written from the post output of a winbuild run and read line by line.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a real control. The reset form `CYCL DEF 32.1` with no T is inferred from the manual (see above).\n- The machine builder must prepare the machine for cycle 32 (the manual says so). The DIN/ISO post already writes `G62` for the Picomax on the same assumption.\n- The other Klartext items of #4095 stay open: other iTNC 530 releases (#4114), `TOOL CALL \"NAME\"`, `FUNCTION DWELL`, and an M91/M92 retract where `m140` is no. The Klartext post still serves NC 340490-03 only.\n\nChangelog: The Heidenhain Klartext post writes a smoothing ask as cycle 32 TOLERANCE (CYCL DEF 32.0/32.1, and 32.2 HSC-MODE where the control profile and its options permit it), and resets it at the end of each operation. Before, it refused smoothing.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #4095\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
